    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `ask_with_audit` in `app/audit.py`, and it returns the right values against a faked HTTP response.\n\n```python\ndef ask_with_audit(client: Anthropic, prompt: str) -> dict:\n    raw = client.messages.with_raw_response.create(\n        model=MODEL, max_tokens=256, messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}]\n    )\n    message = raw.parse()\n    return {\n        \"request_id\": raw.headers.get(\"request-id\"),\n        \"raw_body\": raw.text(),\n        \"answer\": \"\".join(block.text for block in message.content if block.type == \"text\"),\n    }\n```\n\n- **`raw.text()` is a method call.** In the pinned SDK version (anthropic 1.8.0), `.text` is a method, not a property as it was in 0.x, so writing `raw.text` would put a bound method into the audit log instead of the body. I checked this in the installed SDK.\n- **Missing header:** if the `request-id` header is absent, `request_id` comes back as `None` instead of raising an error.\n- **Same shape as the existing code:** the `answer` logic matches `app/assistant.py`, and no dependencies were added.\n\n**Testing:** `pytest -q` passes (1 test), but that test only checks that `MODEL` starts with `claude-`; it never calls the function. So I also ran it offline against a faked HTTP response containing two text blocks. It returned the request ID `req_abc`, the joined answer `Hello`, and a `raw_body` that exactly matched the body sent. Nothing was sent to the real API.\n\n**Leftover file:** that check lives in `_scratch_check.py` in the project root. My command to delete it needed approval and didn't run, so please delete it (or I can turn it into a proper test under `tests/` if you want this covered)."
  },
